Given a square grid composed of black and white cells, labeled Original in the image, perform a one-time fold along the red axis as indicated by the red arrow.

Folding rules are as follows:
1. Mirror and fold the part of the image on the base side of the arrow across the red line, and overlay it onto the tip side of the arrow;
2. If a cell is covered by multiple black cells during the fold, it remains black (black pixels are merged);
3. White cells do not override black cells — all black pixels must be preserved after folding.

From the given options (A–E), select the pattern that correctly represents the result after folding.

